 "overview": "The Medford Bicycle Advisory Commission is a civic body that advises the city on bicycle infrastructure, safety, and public outreach. Since 2022, the commission has worked to expand Medford's bicycle network through new lanes, bike-share stations, and dedicated multi-use paths like the Clippership Connector. The body also coordinates the procurement and distribution of safety equipment, such as lights and helmets, and advocates for safety improvements on state-controlled roadways. As of late 2026, the commission is focused on strategic goals involving contraflow lanes, membership recruitment, and establishing formal safety reporting protocols with the police department.",
 "threads": [
  {
   "name": "Bicycle Lane Network and Infrastructure",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The commission has overseen the rollout of major on-street infrastructure, beginning with the review of a draft bicycle network map in late 2022. Early projects focused on Winthrop Street and Salem Street, including design refinements for bus stop interfaces and parking impacts. By 2026, the work evolved to include contraflow lane installations on Park Street and the evaluation of potential bike lanes on Lawrence Road and Fulton Street. The body consistently reviews city repaving schedules to identify opportunities for adding bicycle facilities during routine maintenance.",
