   "name": "State Roadway Advocacy",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The body frequently advocates for safety improvements on roadways controlled by state agencies like MassDOT and the DCR. Early efforts included responding to fatal crashes on Middlesex Avenue and reviewing the Wellington Circle redesign study to prioritize non-motorized users. The commission has voiced opposition to substandard infrastructure, such as the 2025 repainting of the Route 60 rotary, and requested lower speed limits on state-controlled routes. Efforts are ongoing to coordinate with neighboring towns like Arlington on unified safety marking proposals for border rotaries.",
